cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HxH OCR, its models or its datasets, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HxH OCR: an optical character recogniser for the Hunter x Hunter alphabet"
abstract: >-
  To our knowledge, the first OCR for the Hunter x Hunter alphabet, an invented script that
  is a one-to-one cipher for Japanese kana. A DBNet-style line detector and two CTC line
  readers on a MobileNetV4-small backbone, trained only on synthetic data, quantised to int8
  with quantisation-aware training that follows Espressif's ESP-DL rules, and run in the
  browser by a no_std Rust engine compiled to WebAssembly that is bit-exact with ESP-PPQ.
authors:
  - alias: KokkakNiphon
    website: "https://github.com/KokkakNiphon"
repository-code: "https://github.com/KokkakNiphon/hxh-ocr"
url: "https://hxh-ocr.kokkakniphon.workers.dev"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
keywords:
  - OCR
  - text recognition
  - text detection
  - CTC
  - DBNet
  - synthetic data
  - int8 quantisation
  - WebAssembly
  - Hunter x Hunter
